00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:04,110
Overwrite Memory Data!

2455
00:05:06,430 --> 00:05:10,520
Like putting a futon that won't fit in a closet inside a compression bag?

2456
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:12,560
Strictly speaking, it's different.

2457
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:14,730
But that's close enough for you to get an idea.

2458
00:05:14,730 --> 00:05:18,480
Just as with the D-mail, we can send data to the past.

2459
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:22,070
Then we use the cell phone's spread spectrum waves to copy

2460
00:05:22,070 --> 00:05:24,700
the future memories to the brain in the past.

2461
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:27,530
This creates a "you" with memories from the future.

2462
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:31,870
The furthest back you can send data is forty-eight hours at a time.

2463
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:34,540
Any further, and the two brain states'

2464
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:36,630
difference is too large,

2465
00:05:36,630 --> 00:05:38,960
and it might fail.

2466
00:05:40,050 --> 00:05:42,010
And there's one other problem.

2467
00:05:42,010 --> 00:05:42,760
What?

2468
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:45,340
Unlike the Phone Microwave or the D-mail,

2469
00:05:45,340 --> 00:05:47,550
we need an experiment subject,

2470
00:05:48,050 --> 00:05:49,560
or we can't do it.

2471
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:53,020
Since we're sending memories,

2472
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:55,770
the only way to know if it succeeded

2473
00:05:55,770 --> 00:05:57,360
is to use a human.

2474
00:05:57,360 --> 00:06:01,480
In other words, one of us has to do it?

2475
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,990
I'll pass.

2476
00:06:02,990 --> 00:06:05,660
Okabe, tell me what you think.

2477
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:09,080
Not Hououin... Okabe.

2478
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:13,750
Daru?

2479
00:06:13,750 --> 00:06:14,750
'Sup?

2480
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:18,540
We still don't know why the line connected to SERN, right?

2481
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:20,130
Yeah...

2482
00:06:20,130 --> 00:06:22,880
But there's nothing to indicate the hacking has been discovered.

2483
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:25,050
I agree.

2484
00:06:25,050 --> 00:06:28,800
If they'd really noticed, they would have done something.

2485
00:06:33,770 --> 00:06:36,600
Can we really overcome time?

2486
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:38,690
Part of me wants to find out.

2487
00:06:39,810 --> 00:06:41,070
Th-Then...

2488
00:06:41,070 --> 00:06:43,070
Can't Mayushii buy some bananas,

2489
00:06:43,070 --> 00:06:45,700
so we can time leap the bananas that Mayushii bought

2490
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:48,280
Mayuri, I explained, right?

2491
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:49,910
Bananas have no memories.

2492
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:52,080
But we won't do the experiment.

2493
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:57,000
We'll announce this to the world.

2494
00:06:57,710 --> 00:07:00,590
We'll give the time leap machine to an appropriate organization.

2495
00:07:01,210 --> 00:07:03,170
I agree...

2496
00:07:03,670 --> 00:07:05,510
If you're okay with that.

2497
00:07:05,510 --> 00:07:08,800
Mayushii really agrees!

2498
00:07:15,270 --> 00:07:18,140
Hashida ordered pizza, right?

2499
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:19,310
Yeah.

2500
00:07:19,310 --> 00:07:22,610
Then I'll just make the salad.

2501
00:07:22,610 --> 00:07:23,900
And we'll need...

2502
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:24,820
Wait.

2503
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:25,570
What?

2504
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:26,990
You said salad, right?

2505
00:07:26,990 --> 00:07:29,700
Yes, grapefruit salad.

2506
00:07:29,700 --> 00:07:32,330
Then why do we have natto and ground beef in the cart?

2507
00:07:32,330 --> 00:07:34,540
You can make some good stuff by combining things.

2508
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:36,500
The grapefruit is sour, so you can

2509
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:37,910
combine anything with it.

2510
00:07:37,910 --> 00:07:39,500
No, you can't!

2511
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:40,630
You can!

2512
00:07:40,630 --> 00:07:41,920
You'll see, once you try.

2513
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:43,880
If you want salad,

2514
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:45,800
there's a complete salad right here!

2515
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:46,800
And it's 50% off!

2516
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:49,510
It's no fun buying something that's already made.

2517
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:51,090
This is why guys

2518
00:07:51,090 --> 00:07:53,300
only interested in experiments are no good...

2519
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:55,930
Ah, here's the coriander.

2520
00:07:55,930 --> 00:07:56,970
It's me.

2521
00:07:56,970 --> 00:07:59,390
The Organization's agent has finally made her move.

2522
00:07:59,390 --> 00:08:01,020
Send help!

2523
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:02,360
Now!

2524
00:08:04,110 --> 00:08:06,820
You look like a cat just out of the hospital.

2525
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:09,400
Your face says, "I'm free at last!"

2526
00:08:10,030 --> 00:08:11,530
I'm surprised.

2527
00:08:11,530 --> 00:08:14,280
I expected you to say we were starting

2528
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:16,240
the time leap experiment immediately.

2529
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:17,040
Dissatisfied?

2530
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:20,040
I guess so.

2531
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,170
On a fundamental level, humans are temporal creatures.

2532
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:33,680
Heidegger said that.

2533
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:39,890
Honestly, I was relieved when you said we wouldn't do the experiment.

2534
00:08:39,890 --> 00:08:44,020
I think everyone else agrees.

2535
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:46,570
<i>Hey, if we're having a party,</i>

2536
00:08:46,570 --> 00:08:48,650
<i>can I call Ruka-chan and Feyris-chan?</i>

2537
00:08:48,650 --> 00:08:50,740
<i>It's a development conference.</i>

2538
00:08:53,490 --> 00:08:55,700
Mayuri might have been thinking

2539
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:57,870
we should stop, for a long time now.

2540
00:08:58,660 --> 00:08:59,580
That's true.

2541
00:09:00,370 --> 00:09:04,040
Actually, she may have seen more than the two of us,

2542
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:06,670
since we've been obsessed with the experiments.

2543
00:09:09,670 --> 00:09:11,010
When do we announce it?

2544
00:09:11,010 --> 00:09:13,300
The sooner the better, I think.

2545
00:09:13,300 --> 00:09:14,970
Tell me ahead of time.

2546
00:09:14,970 --> 00:09:16,600
I want to contact my mom.

2547
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:18,850
And...

2548
00:09:20,770 --> 00:09:23,190
My dad will also find out

2549
00:09:23,190 --> 00:09:25,690
that I made a time leap machine.

2550
00:09:26,310 --> 00:09:28,650
Maybe we won't be able to go to Aomori.

2551
00:09:28,650 --> 00:09:30,280
This is going to be big.

2552
00:09:31,110 --> 00:09:32,280
Don't worry.

2553
00:09:33,320 --> 00:09:37,580
I'll solve my lab members' problems.

2554
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,790
Right, right.

2555
00:09:41,790 --> 00:09:44,120
You just want to abuse me as your assistant, right?

2556
00:09:44,670 --> 00:09:46,130
Because you're my dear companion.

2557
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:50,420
Th-Thanks...

2558
00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:03,940
Ow...

2559
00:10:03,940 --> 00:10:05,190
What are you doing?

2560
00:10:05,190 --> 00:10:06,600
I thought you might have a fever

2561
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:08,610
because you're saying un-assistant-like things!

2562
00:10:09,070 --> 00:10:10,860
I-I'm not...

2563
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:13,190
I'm not grateful to you.

2564
00:10:13,190 --> 00:10:15,780
I'm just being polite...

2565
00:10:15,780 --> 00:10:17,700
What kind of tsundere is that?

2566
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:18,700
I'm not a tsundere!

2567
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:20,790
And what about you?

2568
00:10:20,790 --> 00:10:23,450
You always, always say the craziest stuff,

2569
00:10:23,450 --> 00:10:25,210
and now you're talking about companions?

2570
00:10:25,210 --> 00:10:26,710
You're all over the place!

2571
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:28,710
Don't be stupid!

2572
00:10:28,710 --> 00:10:29,960
I never waver.

2573
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:31,550
My lab members are my allies,

2574
00:10:31,550 --> 00:10:32,710
and the world my enemy!

2575
00:10:32,710 --> 00:10:34,010
That's all.

2576
00:10:34,510 --> 00:10:36,010
I'm so stunned, I can't speak.

2577
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:38,010
You just spoke!

2578
00:10:39,890 --> 00:10:42,180
Don't try to trip me up!

2579
00:10:45,310 --> 00:10:46,520
Welcome back!

2580
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:48,690
Snacking while everyone's out?

2581
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:50,110
That's bad manners.

2582
00:10:50,110 --> 00:10:51,860
Pizza doesn't taste good cold.

2583
00:10:52,190 --> 00:10:55,070
Anyway, why are all three of them the same?

2584
00:10:55,070 --> 00:10:56,740
My personal taste.

2585
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:57,700
Why, you...

2586
00:10:57,700 --> 00:11:00,530
You think you can be so dictatorial?!

2587
00:11:00,530 --> 00:11:01,490
See?

2588
00:11:01,490 --> 00:11:03,740
I was right to buy the ingredients, wasn't I?

2589
00:11:03,740 --> 00:11:06,040
Wait a second. I'll get started.

2590
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:07,670
Why didn't you stop her?

2591
00:11:07,670 --> 00:11:09,630
I did! With all my might! With all I had!

2592
00:11:09,630 --> 00:11:13,210
Okarin, you said you'd protect your lab members, right?

2593
00:11:13,210 --> 00:11:14,340
Don't give up.

2594
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:16,550
It might not be over yet.

2595
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:17,510
It's still possible

2596
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:19,430
the apple pie was just a failed attempt,

2597
00:11:19,430 --> 00:11:20,800
and normally...

2598
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:21,680
I forgot radishes...

2599
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:23,310
I guess sweet pickles will work.

2600
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:28,140
When this meal is over, I'm going to retire and get married.

2601
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:30,100
I'm back!

2602
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:30,810
Mayuri, I'm so glad.

2603
00:11:30,810 --> 00:11:32,270
Get to the kitchen!

2604
00:11:32,270 --> 00:11:33,610
Yo!

2605
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:35,990
What? I smell something good.

2606
00:11:36,690 --> 00:11:38,530
The pizza's here already?

2607
00:11:38,530 --> 00:11:40,200
I'll get my kara-age...

2608
00:11:46,830 --> 00:11:49,210
Why is Makise Kurisu here?

2609
00:11:49,210 --> 00:11:51,290
Because I'm a lab member.

2610
00:11:51,290 --> 00:11:52,880
What are you doing here?

2611
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:54,340
I'm a lab member.

2612
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:55,630
What's going on?

2613
00:11:55,630 --> 00:11:56,550
No idea.

2614
00:11:57,010 --> 00:11:59,800
Kurisu-chan, did something happen between you and Suzu-san?

2615
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:00,840
Nothing.

2616
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:03,890
She just keeps blaming me for the craziest stuff.

2617
00:12:03,890 --> 00:12:05,310
She said I'm a SERN spy.

2618
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000


2619
00:12:05,310 --> 00:12:07,430
I'm not crazy. It's the truth.

2620
00:12:07,430 --> 00:12:09,730
How can you be so certain?

2621
00:12:09,730 --> 00:12:10,640
Do you have any proof?

2622
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:12,100
I don't have any proof.

2623
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:13,190
But it will happen.

2624
00:12:13,190 --> 00:12:13,770
Huh?

2625
00:12:13,770 --> 00:12:15,400
It's a prophecy.

2626
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:18,440
I know more about you than you do.

2627
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:20,650
Who you really are,

2628
00:12:20,650 --> 00:12:22,950
and what you're going to do after this.

2629
00:12:23,370 --> 00:12:24,490
I'm sorry.

2630
00:12:24,490 --> 00:12:26,160
That makes so little sense,

2631
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:28,000
I have no idea what you're talking about.

2632
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Kurisu-chan...

2633
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,710
Suzu-san!

2634
00:12:31,710 --> 00:12:34,210
Get back, Mayuri...

2635
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:40,550
Only Hououin Kyouma can handle this situation.

2636
00:12:40,550 --> 00:12:41,550
Assistant!

2637
00:12:41,550 --> 00:12:43,930
I raised you better than that!

2638
00:12:43,930 --> 00:12:45,970
You didn't raise me.

2639
00:12:45,970 --> 00:12:49,640
I'll tell you what the most important thing is about being a mad scientist...

2640
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:51,440
I'm not listening, and I won't be a mad scientist.

2641
00:12:52,310 --> 00:12:53,400
Part-time soldier!

2642
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:55,940
I warned Okabe Rintaro, didn't I?

2643
00:12:55,940 --> 00:12:58,280
Beware of Makise Kurisu.

2644
00:12:58,280 --> 00:13:00,440
Yes, you did say that...

2645
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:02,360
You did, huh?

2646
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:04,570
So you believed her, did you?

2647
00:13:04,570 --> 00:13:06,280
I did not...

2648
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:08,120
But you didn't tell me I was wrong.

2649
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:09,160
Um...

2650
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:10,790
Aren't you making things worse?

2651
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:12,040
Shut up!

2652
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:13,370
Why don't you try?

2653
00:13:13,370 --> 00:13:13,960
You knowâ

2654
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,130
Um...

2655
00:13:15,750 --> 00:13:19,800
Mayushii doesn't like fighting...

2656
00:13:20,760 --> 00:13:21,720
Mayuri.

2657
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:24,760
I-I don't really like it, either.

2658
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:27,140
When we're all together...

2659
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:31,180
I think it'd be more fun if we were friends!

2660
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:47,950
Consider well.

2661
00:13:47,950 --> 00:13:49,410
Is that card a link?

2662
00:13:49,410 --> 00:13:50,620
Or a virus?

2663
00:13:50,620 --> 00:13:54,000
Part-time soldier, your fate as a soldier,

2664
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,920
and the last slice of cake, rests on this.

2665
00:13:58,290 --> 00:13:59,750
When in doubt, attack!

2666
00:13:59,750 --> 00:14:02,470
That's my motto!

2667
00:14:07,390 --> 00:14:09,140
You fell for it, girl.

2668
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:11,180
Now you have three viruses.

2669
00:14:11,180 --> 00:14:13,270
Tell me you give up,

2670
00:14:13,270 --> 00:14:15,390
and I'll give you the cherry on top.

2671
00:14:15,850 --> 00:14:17,810
Miss Amane is taking this too seriously.

2672
00:14:17,810 --> 00:14:20,320
Okarin, you're being mean to Suzu-san.

2673
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:22,690
In the world of games, it's live or die.

2674
00:14:22,690 --> 00:14:25,200
That's how I was raised.

2675
00:14:25,650 --> 00:14:27,660
The ones lined up in the corner

2676
00:14:27,660 --> 00:14:29,780
are definitely link cards.

2677
00:14:30,330 --> 00:14:33,250
Knowing Okabe's personality, I'm sure of it.

2678
00:14:33,250 --> 00:14:34,580
Take one.

2679
00:14:37,830 --> 00:14:39,170
She's right!

2680
00:14:39,170 --> 00:14:40,210
Assistant!

2681
00:14:40,210 --> 00:14:42,510
You're my assistant, yet you betray me?

2682
00:14:42,510 --> 00:14:43,880
Stop calling me assistant!

2683
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:46,220
I hate that arrogance of yours!

2684
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:49,090
I... I won't thank you.

2685
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:52,180
Mayushii will help, too.

2686
00:14:52,180 --> 00:14:55,680
Then would you get tea for everyone, Mayuri?

2687
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:56,600
Sure!

2688
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:57,940
Now then...

2689
00:14:58,810 --> 00:15:00,690
Thank you, Kurisu-chan.

2690
00:15:00,690 --> 00:15:01,860
For what?

2691
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:05,610
Mayushii is happy you made friends with Suzu-san.

2692
00:15:07,110 --> 00:15:09,910
We're not really friends.

2693
00:15:09,910 --> 00:15:12,580
But I think you're right.

2694
00:15:13,040 --> 00:15:16,750
When we're all together, it's more fun to get along.

2695
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:20,210
I was talking with Okabe...

2696
00:15:20,710 --> 00:15:22,290
You may be the one

2697
00:15:22,290 --> 00:15:25,630
with the clearest view of the lab.

2698
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:31,640
That was the only time Okabe's looked serious.

2699
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:33,720
It was kind of creepy.

2700
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:35,640
That's mean to Okarin!

2701
00:15:35,640 --> 00:15:36,350
I'm sorry.

2702
00:15:36,350 --> 00:15:37,230
But...

2703
00:15:37,810 --> 00:15:40,980
Curse you, part-time warrior!

2704
00:15:40,980 --> 00:15:42,900
You won, but not of your own ability!

2705
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:44,110
Don't be so arrogant!

2706
00:15:44,110 --> 00:15:46,440
This is really good!

2707
00:15:47,070 --> 00:15:48,820
I'm off to plan for round two.

2708
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:52,070
Enjoy it while you can...

2709
00:15:52,070 --> 00:15:54,030
The last dessert of your life!

2710
00:15:56,370 --> 00:15:57,750
Wanna go check on him?

2711
00:15:57,750 --> 00:15:59,920
I'll take care of this.

2712
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:01,420
Okay.

2713
00:16:09,220 --> 00:16:11,930
Okarin!

2714
00:16:12,550 --> 00:16:14,140
What?

2715
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:16,970
I couldn't find a flashlight.

2716
00:16:16,970 --> 00:16:20,940
The Cyalume Saber is Future Gadget #6.

2717
00:16:20,940 --> 00:16:22,400
Don't use it as a flashlight.

2718
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:25,440
But it's bright...

2719
00:16:31,910 --> 00:16:33,120
You seem to be having fun.

2720
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:34,910
I am!

2721
00:16:34,910 --> 00:16:36,790
The pizza was good,

2722
00:16:36,790 --> 00:16:39,500
and Suzu-san and Kurisu-chan were having fun.

2723
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:41,540
I'm not!

2724
00:16:46,050 --> 00:16:48,960
Hey, we've got lots of lab members now, right?

2725
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:52,340
So I was thinking that lately, 
we've been lacking a bunch of stuff.

2726
00:16:52,340 --> 00:16:53,840
A bunch of stuff?

2727
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:55,760
Um, chairs?

2728
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:58,310
And we need more utensils...

2729
00:16:58,310 --> 00:17:00,020
Wait just a bit more.

2730
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:02,230
If we announce we've made a time leap machine,

2731
00:17:02,230 --> 00:17:04,940
we'll get some kind of reward.

2732
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:06,570
That will solve everything.

2733
00:17:06,570 --> 00:17:07,940
Really?

2734
00:17:07,940 --> 00:17:09,280
We can buy chairs and utensils?

2735
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:10,820
Yup.

2736
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:13,660
What if I said we could buy those and still have money left over?

2737
00:17:13,660 --> 00:17:15,450
Then a microwave, too!

2738
00:17:15,450 --> 00:17:18,540
I miss being able to heat up my kara-age.

2739
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:20,290
I'll consider it.

2740
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:26,500
It's kind of strange.

2741
00:17:27,130 --> 00:17:31,470
You looked really lonely in the spring.

2742
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:36,510
The lab was always quiet.

2743
00:17:36,510 --> 00:17:39,720
All I could hear was the sound of your computer.

2744
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:45,190
And now there's Daru-kun and Kurisu-chan,

2745
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:49,020
and Ruka-chan, Suzu-san, Moeka-san,

2746
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:54,860
Feyris-chan, and Mr. Braun and Nae-chan...

2747
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:55,780
Mayuri?

2748
00:17:58,330 --> 00:18:00,370
It's okay now, isn't it?

2749
00:18:00,370 --> 00:18:02,620
Even if Mayushii isn't your hostage anymore.

2750
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:11,300
Okarin! Mayushii!

2751
00:18:12,090 --> 00:18:12,920
Big trouble!

2752
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,470
The trains stopped!

2753
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:25,280
Bomb threat? Akihabara in panic.

2754
00:18:16,010 --> 00:18:17,930
For those of you just tuning in,

2755
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:22,470
the following lines have been shut down, due to a bomb threat.

2756
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:24,230
Yamanote Line.

2757
00:18:24,230 --> 00:18:25,100
Soubu Line.

2758
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:27,520
A bomb threat, huh?

2759
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:28,520
What a pain.

2760
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:30,480
I need to call home.

2761
00:18:31,020 --> 00:18:34,900
This party was to celebrate the time leap machine's completion, right?

2762
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:36,320
That's right.

2763
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:37,910
Why mention that now?

2764
00:18:37,910 --> 00:18:39,990
Are you still hacking into SERN?

2765
00:18:39,990 --> 00:18:43,700
I guess you could say that. I got in deeper.

2766
00:18:43,700 --> 00:18:44,870
What do you mean?!

2767
00:18:44,870 --> 00:18:47,330
I got a direct connection to SERN.

2768
00:18:56,340 --> 00:18:58,680
Everyone! You need to...

2769
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:02,680
I'm sorry.

2770
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:03,640
I'm leaving!

2771
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:06,350
Suzu-san!

2772
00:19:07,100 --> 00:19:09,350
What was that about?

2773
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:11,110
What will you do, Mayushii?

2774
00:19:11,110 --> 00:19:12,570
Take a taxi home?

2775
00:19:12,570 --> 00:19:16,070
Hmm... Don't have the money for a taxi.

2776
00:19:37,090 --> 00:19:38,880
Huh?

2777
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:42,640
My watch isn't working...

2778
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:44,640
That's strange.

2779
00:19:44,970 --> 00:19:48,850
I just wound it.

2780
00:20:00,660 --> 00:20:02,240
What is this?

2781
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:04,410
Wh-What?

2782
00:20:04,410 --> 00:20:06,620
...have been suspended...

2783
00:20:07,410 --> 00:20:08,790
Don't move.

2784
00:20:08,790 --> 00:20:10,420
All of you, put your hands up.

2785
00:20:35,980 --> 00:20:37,320
Moeka-san...

2786
00:20:38,240 --> 00:20:40,530
Kiryuu Moeka...

2787
00:20:42,610 --> 00:20:44,910
SERN will take the time machine.

2788
00:20:45,370 --> 00:20:46,620
SERN?

2789
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:47,830
What do you mean?

2790
00:20:48,950 --> 00:20:50,660
Makise Kurisu.

2791
00:20:50,660 --> 00:20:52,120
Okabe Rintaro.

